ion of globally charged black-hole states coexist with a sensible quantum theory of gravity?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0024"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:39e9759117a2adf0a16deaed0d48755883338f1cedb0e11ce35d23f0a197204a","title":"Can fermion bilinears sourcing nondynamical torsion replace the big bang with a classical nonsingular bounce, while supporting viable background evolution and stable cosmological perturbations?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0026"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:3947265a02602d4ead1f5677bb7f9cf93b83dd37f3af973db538c2343acfe91a","title":"Under what assumptions do higher-dimension operators increase black-hole entropy at fixed mass and charge, and can the resulting coefficient bounds enforce a positive extremality shift and the weak gravity conjecture?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0027"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:399545e5a88bee4dd879113c4497f58c7669311b06ecafa112991aa3545f5664","title":"Does the protection survive when quintessence itself propagates in a loop? A linear matter potential makes that failure accessible at one loop, while the source places the analogous massive quadratic-matter corrections at two loops.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0036"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:3932aaff54f8a52b0e5b64206215ea8fe809267cabe666ea9171a5dd2ebf9679","title":"Can six-dimensional generic representation types motivate common matter in four-dimensional F-theory?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0038"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:39b4ed995aa552bf3d1e09f545ec0ad36a5a947f546240f70a3bac1c09ff7a5b","title":"Do towers generate infinite-distance metrics through emergence, and can D-instanton corrections instead place the boundaries 